plan.md.template — the contract for an spp task.

Produced by:  the designer agent during /spp-init (DESIGN.md §4.1).
Consumed by:  /spp-baseline, /spp-loop, /spp-finalize. Each command
              re-reads this file fresh and verifies its actions are
              still on-spec.
Mid-task changes:  append a dated entry to "Plan revision log" below
                   with the reason. Do not silently rewrite earlier
                   sections — the contract's history is part of its
                   value.

Placeholder syntax: {{PLACEHOLDER_NAME}}. Each placeholder has an
inline HTML comment describing what fills it, by whom, at what stage.
The Phase 4 template linter (tests/) will verify all placeholders are
resolved before the file is treated as a final plan.

Glossary terms (baseline overfitting, model overfitting, sacred test
set, auditor information isolation, categorical/row-specific rule
edit, HITL gate, plan.md as contract) are defined in DESIGN.md §10
and are referenced here without redefinition.

This template is v0.2 forward (DESIGN.md §7.1.1 compat layer):
§2 holds OUTPUT_SCHEMA + per-field definitions; §4 holds an
aggregate-strategy block + per-field metric sub-blocks + per-field
floor sub-blocks. Existing v0.1.0 plans (LABEL_SPACE + scalar
metric fields) continue to work without modification — the
runner's K=1 fallback auto-promotes them at read time. Users who
want to migrate an existing v0.1.0 plan to the v0.2 template
surface follow the manual upgrade steps documented in DESIGN.md
§7.1.1 compat layer.
-->

