## 3. Success criteria

**Production decision rule** (the threshold or rule the prompt's
output drives):
{{DECISION_RULE}}
<!-- DECISION_RULE: e.g. "any ticket classified Billing routes to the
     billing team; everything else stays in general queue." This is
     what the metric must support, not the metric itself. -->

**Headline success criterion** (the single aggregate number the user
cares about most; per DESIGN.md §7.1.1 metrics layer decision 4 the
aggregate metric is what /spp-loop's stop discipline gates against):
{{AGGREGATE_METRIC_TARGET}}
<!-- AGGREGATE_METRIC_TARGET: e.g. "aggregate F1 ≥ 0.85 on test",
     "aggregate macro-F1 ≥ 0.80". Drives the per-field metric +
     aggregate-strategy choice in §4. Under K=1 (single-output
     classification) the aggregate equals the lone field's metric
     (any aggregate strategy is the identity); a v0.1.0-shaped
     "F1 ≥ 0.85" criterion is equivalent to the K=1 target. -->

**Acceptable trade-offs:**
{{TRADEOFF_NOTES}}
<!-- TRADEOFF_NOTES: what the user is willing to give up. E.g.
     "willing to accept 5% precision drop for 10% recall gain because
