## 8. Loop scope and stop criteria

**spp scope:** {{SPP_SCOPE}}
<!-- SPP_SCOPE: one of {full, stripped-no-phase3,
     stripped-judge-metric}. The designer's deepest job is figuring
     out which version applies (DESIGN.md core principle 2 +
     §4.1). "full" = canonical Phase 1 + 1.5 + 2 + 3. Stripped
     versions document what is being skipped and why. -->

**MAX_ITERATIONS:** {{MAX_ITERATIONS}}
<!-- MAX_ITERATIONS: hard ceiling on Phase 2 iterations. Default 12;
     stripped scopes may go lower. -->

**Dev plateau threshold:** {{DEV_PLATEAU_THRESHOLD}}
<!-- DEV_PLATEAU_THRESHOLD: e.g. "<0.005 improvement for 3
     consecutive iterations." Loop stops when this is met. -->

**Overfitting early-stop guard:** {{OVERFIT_GUARD}}
<!-- OVERFIT_GUARD: train-vs-dev divergence threshold that triggers
     stop. E.g. "train F1 - dev F1 > 0.10 for 2 consecutive
     iterations." -->

**Auditor configuration:** {{AUDITOR_CONFIG}}
<!-- AUDITOR_CONFIG: required value "per-iteration, no-score-access".
     This is non-negotiable per DESIGN.md §4.2. The plan template
     enforces the value rather than offering a knob — score access
     is forbidden, frequency reduction is forbidden. -->

**Adversary:** {{ADVERSARY_FLAG}}
<!-- ADVERSARY_FLAG: one of {on, off}. Optional sub-component
     (DESIGN.md §4.3). On for high-stakes tasks. -->

